{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011vbpDigLkAERsALQS3dnpQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full experiment plan. Let me identify all the \"planned\" experiments:\n\n- plan_004: GPT-2 SVA K=3 CSS\n- plan_005: GPT-2 DocQA/Factual K=3 CSS\n- plan_006: Qwen-2.5 0.5B IOI K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + IFR)\n- plan_007: Qwen-2.5 0.5B Arithmetic K=3\n\n\n- plan_008: Gemma-2 2B IOI K=3\n- plan_009: Llama-3.1 8B IOI K=3\n- plan_010: Binarization sensitivity ablation\n- plan_011: Ablation method comparison (zero vs mean vs resample)\n- plan_012: CIRCUS as negative ablation\n- plan_013: Jaccard-CSS correlation analysis\n\nNow I need to generate detailed worst-tier predictions for each of these experiments. Let me think through each one carefully based on the worst-tier definition. The core assumption is that SVA max Jaccard exceeds 0.50 as a gradient.\n\nI'm working through the worst-tier framework: gradient methods show systematic correlation regardless of task, CSS with SVA equals 1.0 but underperforms the best single method, similarity-based approaches like IFR and EAP-IG degenerate into gradient proxies at GPT-2 scale, CSS only works reliably on IOI due to its unique localized circuit structure, and the Jaccard-utility relationship is confounded by ACDC binarization—removing it reveals K=2 consensus is hollow. Looking at the expected metric ranges across these experiments: total tasks between 3-4, CSS wins limited to 1 task, SVA max Jaccard spanning 0.45-0.75, and CSS advantage potentially negative.\n\nThe paper direction is shifting away from a methods contribution toward an analysis piece examining when cross-method consensus breaks down in circuit discovery. The core findings would be documenting the systematic correlation among gradient methods, cataloging the pathologies introduced by ACDC binarization, and establishing Jaccard similarity as a necessary but insufficient condition for meaningful consensus. This is better suited for EMNLP Findings or a workshop venue.\n\nNow I'm setting up the detailed predictions for the SVA K=3 CSS experiment on GPT-2 Small.\n\nFor the SVA case, I'm expecting the circuit won't be well-localized either, so gradient methods will show high correlation. The pairwise Jaccard similarities should show eapig and ep methods agreeing around 0.55, but ACDC diverging significantly at 0.15 and 0.12 respectively. The maximum Jaccard stays above the 0.50 threshold, with roughly 15-20 edges achieving full consensus, though ACDC's infinite values dominate. The mean ablation CPR for consensus edges reaches about 0.90, which is respectable but trails what a single gradient method would achieve. This pattern mirrors the Arithmetic failure case, suggesting the same condition④ breakdown is occurring.\n\nFor the DocQA task on GPT-2, I'm anticipating that distributed computation will naturally drive high Jaccard similarities across methods even in the best scenario. The maximum Jaccard likely climbs to 0.60-0.70, and the consensus CPR degrades relative to individual methods, confirming the CSS approach struggles here without revealing anything fundamentally new beyond what Arithmetic already demonstrated.\n\nWith Qwen-2.5 0.5B on IOI, replacing ACDC with IFR should theoretically help, but the similarity-based approach still ends up correlating strongly with gradient methods—Jaccard exceeds 0.50 again. The consensus CPR performance mirrors what we saw with IOI on GPT-2 without clear improvement, though the IOI task itself remains positive.\n\nThe result might hold weakly because IOI's localized structure provides some advantage. Switching to Arithmetic on the same model with IFR will likely show the same pattern: high Jaccard and CSS failing to recover. Scaling up to Gemma-2 2B on IOI should make the circuit less localized, pushing Jaccard higher and eroding CSS's edge. The 8B Llama model will probably follow the same trajectory but more pronounced. Finally, testing binarization sensitivity across different k values shows CSS remains stable, but the absolute CPR advantage doesn't shift—suggesting binarization itself might be a confounding factor driving the results.\n\nComparing ablation methods is critical because mean ablation could artificially inflate CPR for both CSS and single methods, while zero ablation breaks everything, making the CSS advantage entirely method-dependent. CIRCUS already failed on this task, so running it again just confirms the negative result. Looking at the Jaccard-CSS correlation with only one positive task out of three or four gives me a weak relationship—Spearman around 0.3, which isn't statistically significant with so few data points.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6900,"cache_read_input_tokens":21538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6900},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc09ebfc-ff12-4d57-a5a3-2294962bcf00","uuid":"673ddee7-855f-451f-9699-be6f0d3b904a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011vbpDigLkAERsALQS3dnpQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full experiment plan with 10 planned experiments. Let me generate the worst-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Method paper 不可行。Gradient-based methods (EAP-IG, EP) 在 GPT-2 上系统性高相关（Jaccard 0.50-0.70），\n  K=3 的有效独立方法数 K_eff≈1.5。IFR 未能打破这一退化——在 GPT-2 scale 上 similarity-based attribution\n  收敛到 gradient proxy。唯一正面结果 IOI 是 outlier（14-edge ACDC 强先验 + 极端 localized circuit）。\n  Jaccard-utility 关系仅有 3-4 个数据点且被 ACDC binarization confound 驱动，去除 ACDC 后 K=2 consensus\n  无统计意义。重构为 analysis paper: 'When Does Cross-Method Consensus Fail in Circuit Discovery?'\n  投 EMNLP Findings 或 workshop。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # === Task Coverage ===\n  - name: \"GPT-2 SVA K=3 CSS\"\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      Subject-Verb Agreement on GPT-2 Small, K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + ACDC)。\n      验证 CSS 在第三个任务上的表现。SVA 电路预期比 IOI 更 localized，\n      但 worst 档假设 gradient methods 在 GPT-2 上的相关性是系统性的，不因任务而异。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.55\n        eapig_x_acdc: 0.14\n        ep_x_acdc: 0.11\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.55\n      three_way_ratio: 0.09\n      circuit_sizes:\n        eapig: 100\n        ep: 100\n        acdc: 19\n      acdc_binarization: \"isinf (19 edges)\"\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 42\n        \"2/3\": 58\n        \"3/3\": 19\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00_isinf:\n          edges: 19\n          CPR: 0.91\n          CMD: 0.12\n        css_1.00_k50:\n          edges: 38\n          CPR: 0.88\n          CMD: 0.18\n        eapig_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.95\n          CMD: 0.07\n        ep_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.93\n          CMD: 0.10\n        acdc_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.87\n          CMD: 0.19\n      faithfulness_zero:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 19\n          CPR: -0.05\n          CMD: 1.08\n        eap_ig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: -0.03\n          CMD: 1.04\n      d025_verdict: \"FAIL (condition④: CSS=1.0 mean CPR=0.88 < EAP-IG=0.95)\"\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.45\n    result_rationale: >\n      SVA 虽然传统上被认为是 localized circuit，但在 GPT-2 Small 上 EAP-IG 和 EP\n      同为 gradient-based，共享相同的 backward pass 信息——两者识别的 top-100 edges\n      有 55% 重叠。这不是偶然，而是因为 GPT-2 的 12 层 12 头结构中，\n      subject-verb 信息流经的 attention pattern 对 gradient magnitude 和 edge pruning score\n      产生高度相似的排序。ACDC isinf 仅保留 19 条极端边，CSS=1.0≡ACDC，\n      top-k 归一化后 CSS=1.0 (38 edges) 的 CPR=0.88 仍低于 EAP-IG 单方法的 0.95，\n      因为 consensus 丢弃了 EAP-IG 独有的 12 条高贡献边（这些边 EP 未覆盖因其 pruning\n      criterion 对 indirect effects 的敏感度不同）。重复了 Arithmetic 的负面模式。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: SVA pairwise Jaccard matrix (GPT-2 Small, k=100)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"\", \"EAP-IG\", \"EP\", \"ACDC\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"1.00\", \"0.55\", \"0.14\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"0.55\", \"1.00\", \"0.11\"]\n          - [\"ACDC\", \"0.14\", \"0.11\", \"1.00\"]\n      - caption: \"Table: SVA CSS faithfulness comparison (mean ablation, k=50)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CMD\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0 (isinf)\", \"19\", \"0.91\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0 (k=50)\", \"38\", \"0.88\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.95\", \"0.07\"]\n          - [\"EP (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.93\", \"0.10\"]\n          - [\"ACDC (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.87\", \"0.19\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SVA CSS distribution bar chart (1/3, 2/3, 3/3) — 右偏分布，3/3 占比 16%，与 Arithmetic 类似\"\n      - \"Fig: SVA edge overlap Venn diagram — EAP-IG∩EP 大区域，ACDC 几乎不重叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      SVA 重复了 Arithmetic 的模式：gradient methods 高相关导致 K_eff≈1.5，\n      CSS 退化为 ACDC 和 gradient-consensus 的交集而非三方独立投票。\n      至此 3 个 GPT-2 任务中仅 IOI 支持 CSS，初步支持 IOI 是 outlier 的假设。\n      对 Claim 2 提供第三个数据点（max Jaccard=0.55 → CSS fails），但 n=3 仍不足以\n      拟合 threshold。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-2 DocQA/Factual K=3 CSS\"\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      在 GPT-2 Small 上运行分布式计算任务（factual recall 或 document QA），\n      K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + ACDC)。预期分布式电路导致更高的 inter-method 相关性。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.62\n        eapig_x_acdc: 0.22\n        ep_x_acdc: 0.19\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.62\n      three_way_ratio: 0.15\n      circuit_sizes:\n        eapig: 100\n        ep: 100\n        acdc: 35\n      acdc_binarization: \"isinf (35 edges) — 分布式任务产生更多 extreme edges\"\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00_k50:\n          edges: 42\n          CPR: 0.82\n          CMD: 0.25\n        eapig_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.91\n          CMD: 0.13\n        ep_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.88\n          CMD: 0.17\n      d025_verdict: \"FAIL (condition④: CSS=1.0 CPR=0.82 < EAP-IG=0.91)\"\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Distributed computation tasks（如 factual recall）在 GPT-2 上涉及 MLP 和多层\n      attention 的广泛交互——不存在像 IOI 那样的 sparse 14-edge bottleneck。\n      所有 gradient-based methods 都会识别出相似的 \"information highway\" 通路，\n      因为 distributed circuits 的 gradient landscape 更平坦，top edges 的排序差异更小。\n      ACDC isinf 产生 35 条边（比 IOI/SVA 多），因为分布式任务中更多边有 extreme attribution。\n      CSS=1.0 丢弃了各方法独有的 task-specific edges，导致 CPR 下降。\n      本实验的价值在于确认 \"distributed circuit → high Jaccard → CSS fail\" 的因果链，\n      但不产生超出 Arithmetic 已有结论的新 insight。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: DocQA faithfulness comparison (mean ablation, k=50)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CMD\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0 (k=50)\", \"42\", \"0.82\", \"0.25\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.91\", \"0.13\"]\n          - [\"EP (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.88\", \"0.17\"]\n          - [\"ACDC (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.84\", \"0.22\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DocQA CSS distribution — 集中在 2/3 和 3/3，分布式电路导致高一致性\"\n    analysis: >\n      第四个数据点进一步确认 pattern 但边际贡献递减。4 个 GPT-2 任务中 3 个 FAIL，\n      仅 IOI PASS。这足以支撑 analysis paper 的 \"CSS fails when methods correlate\" 叙事，\n      但无法支撑 method paper 的 \"CSS is generally useful\" claim。\n      对 Claim 2 的数据点：max_Jaccard=0.62 → CSS CPR advantage = -0.09。\n\n  # === Model Scaling ===\n  - name: \"Qwen-2.5 0.5B IOI K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + IFR)\"\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      首个非 GPT-2 模型。IFR 替代 ACDC 作为第三种方法（不同 algorithmic family）。\n      Worst 档假设 IFR 在 0.5B scale 退化为 gradient proxy。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.48\n        eapig_x_ifr: 0.52\n        ep_x_ifr: 0.45\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.52\n      three_way_ratio: 0.28\n      circuit_sizes:\n        eapig: 100\n        ep: 100\n        ifr: 100\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 28\n        \"2/3\": 72\n        \"3/3\": 48\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 48\n          CPR: 0.08\n          CMD: 0.87\n        eapig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.10\n          CMD: 0.85\n        ep:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.06\n          CMD: 0.90\n        ifr:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.07\n          CMD: 0.89\n      css_1_cpr_vs_best_single: -0.02\n      ioi_css1_cpr_with_ifr: 0.08\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.48\n    result_rationale: >\n      IFR (Iterative Feature Removal) 本质上通过 feature similarity 来评估 edge importance，\n      但在 0.5B transformer 中，feature similarity 的排序与 gradient magnitude 高度相关——\n      因为 transformer 的 residual stream 结构使得 gradient 和 activation similarity\n      对 edge importance 产生相似的排序（Elhage et al. 2021 的 \"privileged basis\" 现象）。\n      Qwen-2.5 0.5B 有 24 层 16 头，IOI circuit 比 GPT-2 更分散（更多层参与），\n      导致 pairwise Jaccard 虽比 GPT-2 IOI (0.31) 高但不如 Arithmetic (0.70)。\n      CSS=1.0 的 48 条边 CPR=0.08 略低于 EAP-IG 的 0.10——差距很小但方向为负，\n      在 edge-efficiency (CPR/edge) 上 CSS 有微弱优势但不显著。\n      IFR 未能提供预期的 \"different family\" 独立性，K_eff 仍约 1.8。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Qwen-2.5 IOI Jaccard matrix (k=100)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"\", \"EAP-IG\", \"EP\", \"IFR\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"1.00\", \"0.48\", \"0.52\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"0.48\", \"1.00\", \"0.45\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"0.52\", \"0.45\", \"1.00\"]\n      - caption: \"Table: Qwen-2.5 IOI faithfulness (mean ablation)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CPR/edge\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"48\", \"0.08\", \"0.00167\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"100\", \"0.10\", \"0.00100\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"100\", \"0.06\", \"0.00060\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"100\", \"0.07\", \"0.00070\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Qwen IOI Jaccard heatmap — 三对 Jaccard 均在 0.45-0.52，无明显 low-correlation pair\"\n      - \"Fig: CPR vs edge count scatter (Qwen IOI) — CSS=1.0 在 Pareto front 上但优势微弱\"\n    analysis: >\n      IFR 的引入未能打破 gradient-method 相关性困境。虽然 IFR 名义上属于不同 algorithmic family，\n      但其在 transformer 上的行为与 gradient methods 高度相关——这是 worst 档的核心假设。\n      IOI 在 Qwen 上 CSS 的 CPR 优势 (-0.02) 处于噪声水平，与 GPT-2 IOI 的明确正面结果\n      (CPR=0.109 vs best single 0.029) 形成鲜明对比。这暗示 GPT-2 IOI 的成功\n      可能依赖于其极端 localized 的 14-edge ACDC circuit（isinf binarization 的产物），\n      而非 consensus 方法的内在优势。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-2.5 0.5B Arithmetic K=3\"\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      Qwen-2.5 0.5B 上的 Arithmetic (Greaterthan)，K=3 with IFR。\n      验证 IFR 是否能在高相关任务上恢复 CSS。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.58\n        eapig_x_ifr: 0.55\n        ep_x_ifr: 0.50\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.58\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 22\n        \"2/3\": 68\n        \"3/3\": 52\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 52\n          CPR: 0.90\n          CMD: 0.15\n        eapig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.97\n          CMD: 0.04\n        ep:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.94\n          CMD: 0.09\n        ifr:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.92\n          CMD: 0.12\n      d025_verdict: \"FAIL (condition④: CSS=1.0 CPR=0.90 < EAP-IG=0.97)\"\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      Arithmetic 在 Qwen 上延续 GPT-2 的高相关模式。IFR 与 EAP-IG 的 Jaccard=0.55\n      证实 similarity-based 方法未能提供独立视角。虽然 Qwen 的 EAP-IG×EP Jaccard (0.58)\n      比 GPT-2 (0.695) 略低（因模型更大、电路更分散），但仍远高于 CSS 有效工作所需的阈值。\n      Arithmetic 作为数值比较任务，其计算通路在所有方法看来都很相似——\n      MLP 中的 magnitude comparison 操作无论用 gradient、pruning 还是 feature removal 来检测，\n      排序都一致。CSS 没有恢复。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Qwen Arithmetic faithfulness (mean ablation)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CMD\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"52\", \"0.90\", \"0.15\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"100\", \"0.97\", \"0.04\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"100\", \"0.94\", \"0.09\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"100\", \"0.92\", \"0.12\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Qwen Arithmetic CSS distribution — 3/3 比例较高 (37%)，反映方法高一致性\"\n    analysis: >\n      Arithmetic 在两个模型上都失败，进一步支持 \"task structure 决定 CSS utility\" 的结论。\n      IFR 对 method diversity 的贡献可以忽略。Worst 档的核心 thesis 成立：\n      在 transformer 上，所有主流 circuit discovery methods 共享底层 gradient 信息，\n      导致 consensus 退化。\n\n  - name: \"Gemma-2 2B IOI K=3\"\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Scale 到 2B 模型 (Gemma-2)。IOI task，K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + IFR)。\n      验证 CSS 在更大模型上是否保持 IOI 的正面结果。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.42\n        eapig_x_ifr: 0.48\n        ep_x_ifr: 0.40\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.48\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 35\n        \"2/3\": 78\n        \"3/3\": 55\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 55\n          CPR: 0.06\n          CMD: 0.91\n        eapig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.07\n          CMD: 0.90\n        ep:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.04\n          CMD: 0.93\n        ifr:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.05\n          CMD: 0.92\n      css_1_cpr_vs_best_single: -0.01\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemma-2 2B 有 26 层 16 头，IOI circuit 比 GPT-2 的 12 层结构更分散。\n      更多参数意味着更多可能的 edge pathways，pairwise Jaccard 自然降低（0.42-0.48），\n      但这种降低是因为 circuit 变大变分散，而非方法真正独立。CSS=1.0 的 55 条边\n      CPR=0.06 与 EAP-IG 的 0.07 差距 -0.01，在统计上不显著。\n      更大模型上 IOI 不再是极端 localized 的 14-edge circuit——\n      GPT-2 上的 \"IOI exception\" 消失了。这强化了 IOI positive result 是 GPT-2 特有\n      artifact 的论点。edge-efficiency (CPR/edge) 上 CSS 仍有优势 (0.00109 vs 0.00070)，\n      但绝对 CPR 差为负。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Gemma-2 IOI faithfulness (mean ablation)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CPR/edge\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"55\", \"0.06\", \"0.00109\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"100\", \"0.07\", \"0.00070\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"100\", \"0.04\", \"0.00040\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"100\", \"0.05\", \"0.00050\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Model scale vs CSS CPR advantage — 从 GPT-2 (+0.08) 到 Qwen (-0.02) 到 Gemma-2 (-0.01)，趋势向零/负\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale up 后 IOI 的 CSS 优势消失。GPT-2 IOI 的 positive result 越来越像 artifact：\n      ACDC isinf 在 GPT-2 上产生极端 sparse circuit (14 edges)，而这 14 条边恰好是\n      高质量的——这是 GPT-2 IOI 特有的幸运巧合，而非 consensus 方法的系统性优势。\n      在更大模型上，没有 ACDC isinf 的极端 sparsity，CSS 就退化为方法交集的 artifact。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.1 8B IOI K=3\"\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      最大规模实验。Llama-3.1 8B，IOI task，K=3。需要 A100 80GB。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.38\n        eapig_x_ifr: 0.44\n        ep_x_ifr: 0.36\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.44\n      circuit_sizes:\n        eapig: 100\n        ep: 100\n        ifr: 100\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 42\n        \"2/3\": 82\n        \"3/3\": 60\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 60\n          CPR: 0.04\n          CMD: 0.94\n        eapig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.05\n          CMD: 0.93\n      css_1_cpr_vs_best_single: -0.01\n      practical_note: \"EP 在 8B 上 GPU memory 紧张，需 gradient checkpointing，运行时间 ~6h\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 模型有 32 层 32 头，edge space 巨大（~100K potential edges）。\n      k=100 只覆盖 edge space 的 0.1%，导致 pairwise Jaccard 自然降低（稀释效应），\n      但这不代表方法独立——它们在各自 top-100 中识别的 functional role (e.g., induction heads,\n      name mover heads) 相同，只是具体 edge indices 因模型结构更大而分散。\n      CSS=1.0 的 60 条边 CPR=0.04 仅与 EAP-IG 差 -0.01。\n      在如此大的模型上，k=100 本身就是 underpowered——所有方法都在极度 undersample，\n      consensus 变得 trivially similar to random intersection。\n      这个实验最大的价值是展示 \"fixed-k consensus doesn't scale\"。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Llama-3.1 8B IOI results summary\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"Max Jaccard\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"60\", \"0.04\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"100\", \"0.05\", \"0.44\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"100\", \"0.03\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"100\", \"0.04\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Jaccard vs model size — Jaccard 随 model size 下降但 CSS advantage 也下降，表明低 Jaccard 是稀释而非真正的方法独立性\"\n    analysis: >\n      8B 实验的 ROI 极低。高 GPU 成本 (24h A100) 仅产生一个不显著的数据点。\n      在 analysis paper 中可作为 \"scaling caveat\" 一段提及，但不值得单独的 figure。\n      Worst 档建议砍掉此实验以节省资源，或降为 appendix-only。\n\n  # === Ablations ===\n  - name: \"Binarization sensitivity ablation\"\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      系统性 top-k sweep (k=50, 75, 100, 150, 200) 在所有 model×task 对上，\n      验证 CSS 在不同 k 下的稳定性。\n    expected_results:\n      ioi_gpt2_css_cpr_by_k:\n        k50: 0.095\n        k75: 0.100\n        k100: 0.105\n        k150: 0.098\n      sva_gpt2_css_cpr_by_k:\n        k50: 0.88\n        k75: 0.87\n        k100: 0.86\n        k150: 0.85\n      arithmetic_gpt2_css_cpr_by_k:\n        k50: 0.919\n        k75: 0.910\n        k100: 0.905\n        k150: 0.895\n      css_stable_across_k: true\n      but_advantage_never_positive_except_ioi: true\n      key_finding: >\n        CSS CPR 在 k=50-150 范围内稳定（std < 0.02），但这仅说明 binarization\n        本身不是 CSS 失败的原因——方法相关性才是。Worst 档的附加发现：\n        ACDC isinf-vs-topk 的 Jaccard 差异驱动了 Jaccard-utility 的虚假关联。\n      acdc_isinf_vs_topk_jaccard_gap:\n        ioi: \"isinf Jaccard=0.09 → topk Jaccard=0.25 (Δ=+0.16)\"\n        arithmetic: \"isinf Jaccard=0.17 → topk Jaccard=0.42 (Δ=+0.25)\"\n        sva: \"isinf Jaccard=0.14 → topk Jaccard=0.35 (Δ=+0.21)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binarization (isinf vs top-k) 直接影响 ACDC 的 circuit size，进而影响 pairwise\n      Jaccard 和 CSS=1.0 的含义。isinf 下 ACDC 极度 sparse（14-35 edges），\n      与 gradient methods 的 Jaccard 极低；top-k 归一化后 Jaccard 显著上升。\n      这意味着之前观察到的 \"low Jaccard → CSS works (IOI)\" 关系中，IOI 的 low Jaccard\n      部分由 isinf binarization 驱动。去除这个 confound 后，IOI 的 max Jaccard\n      从 0.31 上升到约 0.25（top-k normalized，EAP-IG×EP pair），\n      CSS 的优势主要来自 ACDC isinf 的 extreme selection 而非 genuine consensus。\n      这是 worst 档 Jaccard-utility 关系 \"被 confound 驱动\" 假设的关键证据。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: CSS=1.0 CPR across binarization k values\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Task\", \"k=50\", \"k=75\", \"k=100\", \"k=150\", \"Stable?\"]\n          - [\"IOI (GPT-2)\", \"0.095\", \"0.100\", \"0.105\", \"0.098\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"SVA (GPT-2)\", \"0.88\", \"0.87\", \"0.86\", \"0.85\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Arith (GPT-2)\", \"0.919\", \"0.910\", \"0.905\", \"0.895\", \"Yes\"]\n      - caption: \"Table: ACDC binarization method effect on Jaccard\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Task\", \"Jaccard (isinf)\", \"Jaccard (top-k)\", \"Δ\"]\n          - [\"IOI\", \"0.09\", \"0.25\", \"+0.16\"]\n          - [\"Arith\", \"0.17\", \"0.42\", \"+0.25\"]\n          - [\"SVA\", \"0.14\", \"0.35\", \"+0.21\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: CPR vs k for each task — 平坦曲线，CSS stable 但永远不 beat single method (except IOI)\"\n      - \"Fig: ACDC isinf vs top-k Jaccard — 证明 binarization confound\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档下最有分析价值的实验。证明两件事：(1) CSS 对 binarization 稳定——好消息；\n      (2) 但 Jaccard-utility 关系的很大一部分方差由 ACDC binarization choice 解释，\n      而非 genuine method diversity——坏消息。这为 analysis paper 提供了\n      \"ACDC binarization pathology 的完整 taxonomy\" 贡献（Claim 3 的延伸），\n      也是 'When Does Consensus Fail' 叙事的核心技术贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Ablation method comparison (zero vs mean vs resample)\"\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: >\n      在所有 task 上比较 zero ablation、mean ablation、resample ablation 下\n      CSS 的 faithfulness advantage，验证 CSS 优势是否对 evaluation choice robust。\n    expected_results:\n      ioi_gpt2:\n        zero:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.109\n          best_single_cpr: 0.029\n          advantage: 0.080\n        mean:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.095\n          best_single_cpr: 0.088\n          advantage: 0.007\n        resample:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.085\n          best_single_cpr: 0.082\n          advantage: 0.003\n      sva_gpt2:\n        zero:\n          css_1_cpr: -0.05\n          best_single_cpr: -0.03\n          advantage: -0.02\n        mean:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.88\n          best_single_cpr: 0.95\n          advantage: -0.07\n        resample:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.80\n          best_single_cpr: 0.87\n          advantage: -0.07\n      arithmetic_gpt2:\n        zero:\n          css_1_cpr: -0.184\n          best_single_cpr: -0.131\n          advantage: -0.053\n        mean:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.919\n          best_single_cpr: 0.985\n          advantage: -0.066\n        resample:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.85\n          best_single_cpr: 0.92\n          advantage: -0.07\n      key_finding: >\n        IOI 的 CSS 优势在 zero ablation 下最大 (+0.08)，mean ablation 下微弱 (+0.007)，\n        resample 下几乎消失 (+0.003)。其他任务在所有 ablation 下 CSS 都不优。\n        这意味着 IOI positive result 部分依赖于 zero ablation 的破坏性——\n        zero ablation 对小 circuit 更友好（破坏比例更低），放大了 CSS=1.0 的 edge-efficiency 优势。\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero ablation 将 ablated edges 置零，对大 circuit（100 edges）的破坏程度远大于\n      小 circuit（14 edges），因为更多路径被切断。这给了 CSS=1.0 (14 edges) 一个\n      不公平的优势——不是因为它的 edges 更好，而是因为 100-edge circuits 在 zero ablation\n      下 suffer disproportionately。Mean ablation 缓解了这个 bias（替换为 mean 而非 0），\n      导致大小 circuit 的 CPR 趋近。Resample ablation 进一步消除 out-of-distribution\n      artifacts。在 SVA 和 Arithmetic 上，即使在对 CSS 最有利的 zero ablation 下，\n      gradient methods 的高相关性也阻止了 CSS 产生优势。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: CSS advantage across ablation methods\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Task\", \"Zero Δ\", \"Mean Δ\", \"Resample Δ\"]\n          - [\"IOI\", \"+0.080\", \"+0.007\", \"+0.003\"]\n          - [\"SVA\", \"-0.020\", \"-0.070\", \"-0.070\"]\n          - [\"Arithmetic\", \"-0.053\", \"-0.066\", \"-0.070\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Grouped bar chart — CSS CPR advantage by ablation method × task，IOI 的 zero ablation 优势显眼但 mean/resample 下消失\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下此实验揭示 IOI positive result 的第二个 confound（除 ACDC isinf 外）：\n      zero ablation bias。这对 paper 是双刃剑——削弱了唯一的正面证据，\n      但为 analysis paper 提供了 \"evaluation method confounds in circuit faithfulness\"\n      的重要方法论贡献。建议在 paper 中诚实报告并讨论，这种 transparency 反而加分。\n\n  - name: \"CIRCUS as negative ablation\"\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      整理 D021 的 CIRCUS 三次失败结果，作为负面消融实验展示\n      structural consensus (CSS) vs faithfulness scoring (CIRCUS) 的区别。\n    expected_results:\n      circus_ioi_cpr: -0.108\n      circus_sva_cpr: -0.15\n      circus_arithmetic_cpr: -0.12\n      circus_failure_rate: \"3/3 tasks\"\n      css_vs_circus_framing: >\n        CIRCUS 在所有任务上 CPR 为负（比 random circuit 还差），\n        而 CSS 至少在 IOI 上为正。但 worst 档下 CSS 在 3/4 任务上也失败，\n        所以 CSS vs CIRCUS 的对比变成 \"both methods have severe limitations\"\n        而非 \"CSS > CIRCUS\"。\n    result_rationale: >\n      CIRCUS 使用 threshold diversity 在单一方法内部构建 consensus，\n      本质上是在同一 gradient landscape 上做不同切分——不提供新信息。\n      CSS 至少使用了不同方法，但当方法本身相关时也退化。\n      CIRCUS 的完全失败是可预期的：单方法 threshold sweep 生成的 \"diverse\" circuits\n      实际上是 nested sets（k=50 ⊂ k=100 ⊂ k=150），其交集就是最 conservative 的 cut，\n      这不是 consensus 而是 trivial intersection。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: CIRCUS vs CSS faithfulness comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"IOI CPR\", \"SVA CPR\", \"Arith CPR\"]\n          - [\"CIRCUS\", \"-0.108\", \"-0.15\", \"-0.12\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"+0.109\", \"-0.05\", \"-0.184 (zero) / +0.919 (mean)\"]\n          - [\"Best single\", \"+0.029 (zero)\", \"+0.95 (mean)\", \"+0.985 (mean)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: CIRCUS vs CSS CPR across tasks — CIRCUS consistently negative, CSS mixed\"\n    analysis: >\n      CIRCUS 负面结果是 low-hanging fruit——容易写、审稿人会觉得有信息量。\n      在 analysis paper 中定位为 \"what definitely doesn't work\"，\n      与 CSS 的 \"works under specific conditions\" 形成对比。\n      0 GPU hours，纯分析工作，性价比最高的 planned 实验。\n\n  # === Jaccard Prediction ===\n  - name: \"Jaccard-CSS correlation analysis\"\n    plan_id: plan_013\n    description: >\n      跨所有 model×task 对，拟合 max pairwise Jaccard vs CSS faithfulness advantage 的关系。\n      Worst 档下数据点少且关系被 confound 驱动。\n    expected_results:\n      data_points:\n        - {task: \"IOI\", model: \"GPT-2\", max_jaccard: 0.31, css_advantage: 0.080, note: \"isinf ACDC, zero ablation\"}\n        - {task: \"Arithmetic\", model: \"GPT-2\", max_jaccard: 0.695, css_advantage: -0.066, note: \"mean ablation\"}\n        - {task: \"SVA\", model: \"GPT-2\", max_jaccard: 0.55, css_advantage: -0.070, note: \"mean ablation\"}\n        - {task: \"IOI\", model: \"Qwen-0.5B\", max_jaccard: 0.52, css_advantage: -0.020, note: \"with IFR\"}\n        - {task: \"Arithmetic\", model: \"Qwen-0.5B\", max_jaccard: 0.58, css_advantage: -0.070, note: \"with IFR\"}\n        - {task: \"IOI\", model: \"Gemma-2B\", max_jaccard: 0.48, css_advantage: -0.010, note: \"with IFR\"}\n      n_data_points: 6\n      spearman_rho: -0.54\n      spearman_p_value: 0.27\n      pearson_r: -0.61\n      pearson_p_value: 0.20\n      fitted_threshold: \"max_Jaccard < 0.35 for CSS to work\"\n      n_points_below_threshold: 1\n      n_points_above_threshold: 5\n      confound_analysis: >\n        去除 IOI GPT-2 (唯一用 ACDC isinf 且 zero ablation 的数据点) 后：\n        n=5, spearman_rho=-0.30, p=0.62。关系完全不显著。\n        IOI GPT-2 是 influential point (Cook's D > 1.0)，驱动了整个 correlation。\n    result_rationale: >\n      6 个数据点本身就 underpowered（Spearman 需 n≈10 才有检测 ρ=0.6 的 80% power）。\n      Worst 档下唯一的正面点 (IOI GPT-2) 同时有两个 confounds：\n      (1) ACDC isinf 压低了 max_Jaccard（top-k 归一化后 Jaccard 上升到 0.25→仍低，但方向变化）\n      (2) zero ablation 放大了 CSS 的 edge-efficiency 优势。\n      去除这个 influential point 后，剩余 5 个点都在 Jaccard 0.48-0.70 范围内，\n      CSS advantage 都在 [-0.07, -0.01] 范围内——flat line，no correlation。\n      Jaccard-utility 关系变成了 \"one-point story\"，统计上不可信。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Jaccard-CSS correlation data\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Task×Model\", \"Max Jaccard\", \"CSS Advantage\", \"Confounds\"]\n          - [\"IOI×GPT-2\", \"0.31\", \"+0.080\", \"ACDC isinf + zero ablation\"]\n          - [\"SVA×GPT-2\", \"0.55\", \"-0.070\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Arith×GPT-2\", \"0.695\", \"-0.066\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"IOI×Qwen\", \"0.52\", \"-0.020\", \"IFR may ≈ gradient\"]\n          - [\"Arith×Qwen\", \"0.58\", \"-0.070\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"IOI×Gemma\", \"0.48\", \"-0.010\", \"—\"]\n      - caption: \"Table: Correlation robustness\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Analysis\", \"ρ\", \"p-value\", \"n\"]\n          - [\"All points\", \"-0.54\", \"0.27\", \"6\"]\n          - [\"Remove IOI×GPT-2\", \"-0.30\", \"0.62\", \"5\"]\n          - [\"Remove ACDC tasks only\", \"-0.10\", \"0.87\", \"3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot — max Jaccard (x) vs CSS advantage (y)，IOI×GPT-2 是明显的 outlier，其余点 cluster 在右下区域\"\n      - \"Fig: Same scatter with IOI×GPT-2 标记为 hollow circle (confounded)，回归线变平\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档对 Claim 2 (CSS utility predicted by inter-method correlation) 的致命打击。\n      Correlation 在统计上不显著 (p=0.27)，且由单个 confounded data point 驱动。\n      Paper 不能声称 \"Jaccard predicts CSS utility\" 作为 empirical finding——\n      只能作为 \"motivated conjecture\" 或 \"necessary condition hypothesis\"。\n      Analysis paper 的重构方向：Jaccard 是 necessary condition check\n      （max_Jaccard > 0.5 → CSS almost certainly fails），\n      但不是 sufficient condition（max_Jaccard < 0.5 不保证 CSS works，\n      因为只有一个数据点且有 confounds）。\n      这限制了 contribution 的强度，但对 EMNLP Findings 或 workshop 仍可接受——\n      honest negative results 有其学术价值。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6900,"cache_read_input_tokens":21538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6900},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc09ebfc-ff12-4d57-a5a3-2294962bcf00","uuid":"fe0bbed7-dfcd-4efd-af0c-a2fc331a0107"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":259845,"duration_api_ms":260979,"num_turns":3,"result":"Now I have the full experiment plan with 10 planned experiments. Let me generate the worst-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Method paper 不可行。Gradient-based methods (EAP-IG, EP) 在 GPT-2 上系统性高相关（Jaccard 0.50-0.70），\n  K=3 的有效独立方法数 K_eff≈1.5。IFR 未能打破这一退化——在 GPT-2 scale 上 similarity-based attribution\n  收敛到 gradient proxy。唯一正面结果 IOI 是 outlier（14-edge ACDC 强先验 + 极端 localized circuit）。\n  Jaccard-utility 关系仅有 3-4 个数据点且被 ACDC binarization confound 驱动，去除 ACDC 后 K=2 consensus\n  无统计意义。重构为 analysis paper: 'When Does Cross-Method Consensus Fail in Circuit Discovery?'\n  投 EMNLP Findings 或 workshop。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # === Task Coverage ===\n  - name: \"GPT-2 SVA K=3 CSS\"\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      Subject-Verb Agreement on GPT-2 Small, K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + ACDC)。\n      验证 CSS 在第三个任务上的表现。SVA 电路预期比 IOI 更 localized，\n      但 worst 档假设 gradient methods 在 GPT-2 上的相关性是系统性的，不因任务而异。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.55\n        eapig_x_acdc: 0.14\n        ep_x_acdc: 0.11\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.55\n      three_way_ratio: 0.09\n      circuit_sizes:\n        eapig: 100\n        ep: 100\n        acdc: 19\n      acdc_binarization: \"isinf (19 edges)\"\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 42\n        \"2/3\": 58\n        \"3/3\": 19\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00_isinf:\n          edges: 19\n          CPR: 0.91\n          CMD: 0.12\n        css_1.00_k50:\n          edges: 38\n          CPR: 0.88\n          CMD: 0.18\n        eapig_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.95\n          CMD: 0.07\n        ep_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.93\n          CMD: 0.10\n        acdc_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.87\n          CMD: 0.19\n      faithfulness_zero:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 19\n          CPR: -0.05\n          CMD: 1.08\n        eap_ig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: -0.03\n          CMD: 1.04\n      d025_verdict: \"FAIL (condition④: CSS=1.0 mean CPR=0.88 < EAP-IG=0.95)\"\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.45\n    result_rationale: >\n      SVA 虽然传统上被认为是 localized circuit，但在 GPT-2 Small 上 EAP-IG 和 EP\n      同为 gradient-based，共享相同的 backward pass 信息——两者识别的 top-100 edges\n      有 55% 重叠。这不是偶然，而是因为 GPT-2 的 12 层 12 头结构中，\n      subject-verb 信息流经的 attention pattern 对 gradient magnitude 和 edge pruning score\n      产生高度相似的排序。ACDC isinf 仅保留 19 条极端边，CSS=1.0≡ACDC，\n      top-k 归一化后 CSS=1.0 (38 edges) 的 CPR=0.88 仍低于 EAP-IG 单方法的 0.95，\n      因为 consensus 丢弃了 EAP-IG 独有的 12 条高贡献边（这些边 EP 未覆盖因其 pruning\n      criterion 对 indirect effects 的敏感度不同）。重复了 Arithmetic 的负面模式。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: SVA pairwise Jaccard matrix (GPT-2 Small, k=100)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"\", \"EAP-IG\", \"EP\", \"ACDC\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"1.00\", \"0.55\", \"0.14\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"0.55\", \"1.00\", \"0.11\"]\n          - [\"ACDC\", \"0.14\", \"0.11\", \"1.00\"]\n      - caption: \"Table: SVA CSS faithfulness comparison (mean ablation, k=50)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CMD\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0 (isinf)\", \"19\", \"0.91\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0 (k=50)\", \"38\", \"0.88\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.95\", \"0.07\"]\n          - [\"EP (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.93\", \"0.10\"]\n          - [\"ACDC (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.87\", \"0.19\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SVA CSS distribution bar chart (1/3, 2/3, 3/3) — 右偏分布，3/3 占比 16%，与 Arithmetic 类似\"\n      - \"Fig: SVA edge overlap Venn diagram — EAP-IG∩EP 大区域，ACDC 几乎不重叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      SVA 重复了 Arithmetic 的模式：gradient methods 高相关导致 K_eff≈1.5，\n      CSS 退化为 ACDC 和 gradient-consensus 的交集而非三方独立投票。\n      至此 3 个 GPT-2 任务中仅 IOI 支持 CSS，初步支持 IOI 是 outlier 的假设。\n      对 Claim 2 提供第三个数据点（max Jaccard=0.55 → CSS fails），但 n=3 仍不足以\n      拟合 threshold。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-2 DocQA/Factual K=3 CSS\"\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      在 GPT-2 Small 上运行分布式计算任务（factual recall 或 document QA），\n      K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + ACDC)。预期分布式电路导致更高的 inter-method 相关性。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.62\n        eapig_x_acdc: 0.22\n        ep_x_acdc: 0.19\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.62\n      three_way_ratio: 0.15\n      circuit_sizes:\n        eapig: 100\n        ep: 100\n        acdc: 35\n      acdc_binarization: \"isinf (35 edges) — 分布式任务产生更多 extreme edges\"\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00_k50:\n          edges: 42\n          CPR: 0.82\n          CMD: 0.25\n        eapig_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.91\n          CMD: 0.13\n        ep_k50:\n          edges: 50\n          CPR: 0.88\n          CMD: 0.17\n      d025_verdict: \"FAIL (condition④: CSS=1.0 CPR=0.82 < EAP-IG=0.91)\"\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Distributed computation tasks（如 factual recall）在 GPT-2 上涉及 MLP 和多层\n      attention 的广泛交互——不存在像 IOI 那样的 sparse 14-edge bottleneck。\n      所有 gradient-based methods 都会识别出相似的 \"information highway\" 通路，\n      因为 distributed circuits 的 gradient landscape 更平坦，top edges 的排序差异更小。\n      ACDC isinf 产生 35 条边（比 IOI/SVA 多），因为分布式任务中更多边有 extreme attribution。\n      CSS=1.0 丢弃了各方法独有的 task-specific edges，导致 CPR 下降。\n      本实验的价值在于确认 \"distributed circuit → high Jaccard → CSS fail\" 的因果链，\n      但不产生超出 Arithmetic 已有结论的新 insight。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: DocQA faithfulness comparison (mean ablation, k=50)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CMD\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0 (k=50)\", \"42\", \"0.82\", \"0.25\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.91\", \"0.13\"]\n          - [\"EP (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.88\", \"0.17\"]\n          - [\"ACDC (k=50)\", \"50\", \"0.84\", \"0.22\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DocQA CSS distribution — 集中在 2/3 和 3/3，分布式电路导致高一致性\"\n    analysis: >\n      第四个数据点进一步确认 pattern 但边际贡献递减。4 个 GPT-2 任务中 3 个 FAIL，\n      仅 IOI PASS。这足以支撑 analysis paper 的 \"CSS fails when methods correlate\" 叙事，\n      但无法支撑 method paper 的 \"CSS is generally useful\" claim。\n      对 Claim 2 的数据点：max_Jaccard=0.62 → CSS CPR advantage = -0.09。\n\n  # === Model Scaling ===\n  - name: \"Qwen-2.5 0.5B IOI K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + IFR)\"\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      首个非 GPT-2 模型。IFR 替代 ACDC 作为第三种方法（不同 algorithmic family）。\n      Worst 档假设 IFR 在 0.5B scale 退化为 gradient proxy。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.48\n        eapig_x_ifr: 0.52\n        ep_x_ifr: 0.45\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.52\n      three_way_ratio: 0.28\n      circuit_sizes:\n        eapig: 100\n        ep: 100\n        ifr: 100\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 28\n        \"2/3\": 72\n        \"3/3\": 48\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 48\n          CPR: 0.08\n          CMD: 0.87\n        eapig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.10\n          CMD: 0.85\n        ep:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.06\n          CMD: 0.90\n        ifr:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.07\n          CMD: 0.89\n      css_1_cpr_vs_best_single: -0.02\n      ioi_css1_cpr_with_ifr: 0.08\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.48\n    result_rationale: >\n      IFR (Iterative Feature Removal) 本质上通过 feature similarity 来评估 edge importance，\n      但在 0.5B transformer 中，feature similarity 的排序与 gradient magnitude 高度相关——\n      因为 transformer 的 residual stream 结构使得 gradient 和 activation similarity\n      对 edge importance 产生相似的排序（Elhage et al. 2021 的 \"privileged basis\" 现象）。\n      Qwen-2.5 0.5B 有 24 层 16 头，IOI circuit 比 GPT-2 更分散（更多层参与），\n      导致 pairwise Jaccard 虽比 GPT-2 IOI (0.31) 高但不如 Arithmetic (0.70)。\n      CSS=1.0 的 48 条边 CPR=0.08 略低于 EAP-IG 的 0.10——差距很小但方向为负，\n      在 edge-efficiency (CPR/edge) 上 CSS 有微弱优势但不显著。\n      IFR 未能提供预期的 \"different family\" 独立性，K_eff 仍约 1.8。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Qwen-2.5 IOI Jaccard matrix (k=100)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"\", \"EAP-IG\", \"EP\", \"IFR\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"1.00\", \"0.48\", \"0.52\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"0.48\", \"1.00\", \"0.45\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"0.52\", \"0.45\", \"1.00\"]\n      - caption: \"Table: Qwen-2.5 IOI faithfulness (mean ablation)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CPR/edge\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"48\", \"0.08\", \"0.00167\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"100\", \"0.10\", \"0.00100\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"100\", \"0.06\", \"0.00060\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"100\", \"0.07\", \"0.00070\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Qwen IOI Jaccard heatmap — 三对 Jaccard 均在 0.45-0.52，无明显 low-correlation pair\"\n      - \"Fig: CPR vs edge count scatter (Qwen IOI) — CSS=1.0 在 Pareto front 上但优势微弱\"\n    analysis: >\n      IFR 的引入未能打破 gradient-method 相关性困境。虽然 IFR 名义上属于不同 algorithmic family，\n      但其在 transformer 上的行为与 gradient methods 高度相关——这是 worst 档的核心假设。\n      IOI 在 Qwen 上 CSS 的 CPR 优势 (-0.02) 处于噪声水平，与 GPT-2 IOI 的明确正面结果\n      (CPR=0.109 vs best single 0.029) 形成鲜明对比。这暗示 GPT-2 IOI 的成功\n      可能依赖于其极端 localized 的 14-edge ACDC circuit（isinf binarization 的产物），\n      而非 consensus 方法的内在优势。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-2.5 0.5B Arithmetic K=3\"\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      Qwen-2.5 0.5B 上的 Arithmetic (Greaterthan)，K=3 with IFR。\n      验证 IFR 是否能在高相关任务上恢复 CSS。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.58\n        eapig_x_ifr: 0.55\n        ep_x_ifr: 0.50\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.58\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 22\n        \"2/3\": 68\n        \"3/3\": 52\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 52\n          CPR: 0.90\n          CMD: 0.15\n        eapig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.97\n          CMD: 0.04\n        ep:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.94\n          CMD: 0.09\n        ifr:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.92\n          CMD: 0.12\n      d025_verdict: \"FAIL (condition④: CSS=1.0 CPR=0.90 < EAP-IG=0.97)\"\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      Arithmetic 在 Qwen 上延续 GPT-2 的高相关模式。IFR 与 EAP-IG 的 Jaccard=0.55\n      证实 similarity-based 方法未能提供独立视角。虽然 Qwen 的 EAP-IG×EP Jaccard (0.58)\n      比 GPT-2 (0.695) 略低（因模型更大、电路更分散），但仍远高于 CSS 有效工作所需的阈值。\n      Arithmetic 作为数值比较任务，其计算通路在所有方法看来都很相似——\n      MLP 中的 magnitude comparison 操作无论用 gradient、pruning 还是 feature removal 来检测，\n      排序都一致。CSS 没有恢复。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Qwen Arithmetic faithfulness (mean ablation)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CMD\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"52\", \"0.90\", \"0.15\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"100\", \"0.97\", \"0.04\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"100\", \"0.94\", \"0.09\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"100\", \"0.92\", \"0.12\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Qwen Arithmetic CSS distribution — 3/3 比例较高 (37%)，反映方法高一致性\"\n    analysis: >\n      Arithmetic 在两个模型上都失败，进一步支持 \"task structure 决定 CSS utility\" 的结论。\n      IFR 对 method diversity 的贡献可以忽略。Worst 档的核心 thesis 成立：\n      在 transformer 上，所有主流 circuit discovery methods 共享底层 gradient 信息，\n      导致 consensus 退化。\n\n  - name: \"Gemma-2 2B IOI K=3\"\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Scale 到 2B 模型 (Gemma-2)。IOI task，K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + IFR)。\n      验证 CSS 在更大模型上是否保持 IOI 的正面结果。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.42\n        eapig_x_ifr: 0.48\n        ep_x_ifr: 0.40\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.48\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 35\n        \"2/3\": 78\n        \"3/3\": 55\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 55\n          CPR: 0.06\n          CMD: 0.91\n        eapig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.07\n          CMD: 0.90\n        ep:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.04\n          CMD: 0.93\n        ifr:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.05\n          CMD: 0.92\n      css_1_cpr_vs_best_single: -0.01\n      method_diversity_1_minus_max_jaccard: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemma-2 2B 有 26 层 16 头，IOI circuit 比 GPT-2 的 12 层结构更分散。\n      更多参数意味着更多可能的 edge pathways，pairwise Jaccard 自然降低（0.42-0.48），\n      但这种降低是因为 circuit 变大变分散，而非方法真正独立。CSS=1.0 的 55 条边\n      CPR=0.06 与 EAP-IG 的 0.07 差距 -0.01，在统计上不显著。\n      更大模型上 IOI 不再是极端 localized 的 14-edge circuit——\n      GPT-2 上的 \"IOI exception\" 消失了。这强化了 IOI positive result 是 GPT-2 特有\n      artifact 的论点。edge-efficiency (CPR/edge) 上 CSS 仍有优势 (0.00109 vs 0.00070)，\n      但绝对 CPR 差为负。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Gemma-2 IOI faithfulness (mean ablation)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"CPR/edge\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"55\", \"0.06\", \"0.00109\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"100\", \"0.07\", \"0.00070\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"100\", \"0.04\", \"0.00040\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"100\", \"0.05\", \"0.00050\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Model scale vs CSS CPR advantage — 从 GPT-2 (+0.08) 到 Qwen (-0.02) 到 Gemma-2 (-0.01)，趋势向零/负\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale up 后 IOI 的 CSS 优势消失。GPT-2 IOI 的 positive result 越来越像 artifact：\n      ACDC isinf 在 GPT-2 上产生极端 sparse circuit (14 edges)，而这 14 条边恰好是\n      高质量的——这是 GPT-2 IOI 特有的幸运巧合，而非 consensus 方法的系统性优势。\n      在更大模型上，没有 ACDC isinf 的极端 sparsity，CSS 就退化为方法交集的 artifact。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.1 8B IOI K=3\"\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      最大规模实验。Llama-3.1 8B，IOI task，K=3。需要 A100 80GB。\n    expected_results:\n      pairwise_jaccard:\n        eapig_x_ep: 0.38\n        eapig_x_ifr: 0.44\n        ep_x_ifr: 0.36\n      max_pairwise_jaccard: 0.44\n      circuit_sizes:\n        eapig: 100\n        ep: 100\n        ifr: 100\n      css_distribution:\n        \"1/3\": 42\n        \"2/3\": 82\n        \"3/3\": 60\n      faithfulness_mean:\n        css_1.00:\n          edges: 60\n          CPR: 0.04\n          CMD: 0.94\n        eapig:\n          edges: 100\n          CPR: 0.05\n          CMD: 0.93\n      css_1_cpr_vs_best_single: -0.01\n      practical_note: \"EP 在 8B 上 GPU memory 紧张，需 gradient checkpointing，运行时间 ~6h\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 模型有 32 层 32 头，edge space 巨大（~100K potential edges）。\n      k=100 只覆盖 edge space 的 0.1%，导致 pairwise Jaccard 自然降低（稀释效应），\n      但这不代表方法独立——它们在各自 top-100 中识别的 functional role (e.g., induction heads,\n      name mover heads) 相同，只是具体 edge indices 因模型结构更大而分散。\n      CSS=1.0 的 60 条边 CPR=0.04 仅与 EAP-IG 差 -0.01。\n      在如此大的模型上，k=100 本身就是 underpowered——所有方法都在极度 undersample，\n      consensus 变得 trivially similar to random intersection。\n      这个实验最大的价值是展示 \"fixed-k consensus doesn't scale\"。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Llama-3.1 8B IOI results summary\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"Edges\", \"CPR\", \"Max Jaccard\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"60\", \"0.04\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"EAP-IG\", \"100\", \"0.05\", \"0.44\"]\n          - [\"EP\", \"100\", \"0.03\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"IFR\", \"100\", \"0.04\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Jaccard vs model size — Jaccard 随 model size 下降但 CSS advantage 也下降，表明低 Jaccard 是稀释而非真正的方法独立性\"\n    analysis: >\n      8B 实验的 ROI 极低。高 GPU 成本 (24h A100) 仅产生一个不显著的数据点。\n      在 analysis paper 中可作为 \"scaling caveat\" 一段提及，但不值得单独的 figure。\n      Worst 档建议砍掉此实验以节省资源，或降为 appendix-only。\n\n  # === Ablations ===\n  - name: \"Binarization sensitivity ablation\"\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      系统性 top-k sweep (k=50, 75, 100, 150, 200) 在所有 model×task 对上，\n      验证 CSS 在不同 k 下的稳定性。\n    expected_results:\n      ioi_gpt2_css_cpr_by_k:\n        k50: 0.095\n        k75: 0.100\n        k100: 0.105\n        k150: 0.098\n      sva_gpt2_css_cpr_by_k:\n        k50: 0.88\n        k75: 0.87\n        k100: 0.86\n        k150: 0.85\n      arithmetic_gpt2_css_cpr_by_k:\n        k50: 0.919\n        k75: 0.910\n        k100: 0.905\n        k150: 0.895\n      css_stable_across_k: true\n      but_advantage_never_positive_except_ioi: true\n      key_finding: >\n        CSS CPR 在 k=50-150 范围内稳定（std < 0.02），但这仅说明 binarization\n        本身不是 CSS 失败的原因——方法相关性才是。Worst 档的附加发现：\n        ACDC isinf-vs-topk 的 Jaccard 差异驱动了 Jaccard-utility 的虚假关联。\n      acdc_isinf_vs_topk_jaccard_gap:\n        ioi: \"isinf Jaccard=0.09 → topk Jaccard=0.25 (Δ=+0.16)\"\n        arithmetic: \"isinf Jaccard=0.17 → topk Jaccard=0.42 (Δ=+0.25)\"\n        sva: \"isinf Jaccard=0.14 → topk Jaccard=0.35 (Δ=+0.21)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binarization (isinf vs top-k) 直接影响 ACDC 的 circuit size，进而影响 pairwise\n      Jaccard 和 CSS=1.0 的含义。isinf 下 ACDC 极度 sparse（14-35 edges），\n      与 gradient methods 的 Jaccard 极低；top-k 归一化后 Jaccard 显著上升。\n      这意味着之前观察到的 \"low Jaccard → CSS works (IOI)\" 关系中，IOI 的 low Jaccard\n      部分由 isinf binarization 驱动。去除这个 confound 后，IOI 的 max Jaccard\n      从 0.31 上升到约 0.25（top-k normalized，EAP-IG×EP pair），\n      CSS 的优势主要来自 ACDC isinf 的 extreme selection 而非 genuine consensus。\n      这是 worst 档 Jaccard-utility 关系 \"被 confound 驱动\" 假设的关键证据。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: CSS=1.0 CPR across binarization k values\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Task\", \"k=50\", \"k=75\", \"k=100\", \"k=150\", \"Stable?\"]\n          - [\"IOI (GPT-2)\", \"0.095\", \"0.100\", \"0.105\", \"0.098\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"SVA (GPT-2)\", \"0.88\", \"0.87\", \"0.86\", \"0.85\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Arith (GPT-2)\", \"0.919\", \"0.910\", \"0.905\", \"0.895\", \"Yes\"]\n      - caption: \"Table: ACDC binarization method effect on Jaccard\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Task\", \"Jaccard (isinf)\", \"Jaccard (top-k)\", \"Δ\"]\n          - [\"IOI\", \"0.09\", \"0.25\", \"+0.16\"]\n          - [\"Arith\", \"0.17\", \"0.42\", \"+0.25\"]\n          - [\"SVA\", \"0.14\", \"0.35\", \"+0.21\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: CPR vs k for each task — 平坦曲线，CSS stable 但永远不 beat single method (except IOI)\"\n      - \"Fig: ACDC isinf vs top-k Jaccard — 证明 binarization confound\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档下最有分析价值的实验。证明两件事：(1) CSS 对 binarization 稳定——好消息；\n      (2) 但 Jaccard-utility 关系的很大一部分方差由 ACDC binarization choice 解释，\n      而非 genuine method diversity——坏消息。这为 analysis paper 提供了\n      \"ACDC binarization pathology 的完整 taxonomy\" 贡献（Claim 3 的延伸），\n      也是 'When Does Consensus Fail' 叙事的核心技术贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Ablation method comparison (zero vs mean vs resample)\"\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: >\n      在所有 task 上比较 zero ablation、mean ablation、resample ablation 下\n      CSS 的 faithfulness advantage，验证 CSS 优势是否对 evaluation choice robust。\n    expected_results:\n      ioi_gpt2:\n        zero:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.109\n          best_single_cpr: 0.029\n          advantage: 0.080\n        mean:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.095\n          best_single_cpr: 0.088\n          advantage: 0.007\n        resample:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.085\n          best_single_cpr: 0.082\n          advantage: 0.003\n      sva_gpt2:\n        zero:\n          css_1_cpr: -0.05\n          best_single_cpr: -0.03\n          advantage: -0.02\n        mean:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.88\n          best_single_cpr: 0.95\n          advantage: -0.07\n        resample:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.80\n          best_single_cpr: 0.87\n          advantage: -0.07\n      arithmetic_gpt2:\n        zero:\n          css_1_cpr: -0.184\n          best_single_cpr: -0.131\n          advantage: -0.053\n        mean:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.919\n          best_single_cpr: 0.985\n          advantage: -0.066\n        resample:\n          css_1_cpr: 0.85\n          best_single_cpr: 0.92\n          advantage: -0.07\n      key_finding: >\n        IOI 的 CSS 优势在 zero ablation 下最大 (+0.08)，mean ablation 下微弱 (+0.007)，\n        resample 下几乎消失 (+0.003)。其他任务在所有 ablation 下 CSS 都不优。\n        这意味着 IOI positive result 部分依赖于 zero ablation 的破坏性——\n        zero ablation 对小 circuit 更友好（破坏比例更低），放大了 CSS=1.0 的 edge-efficiency 优势。\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero ablation 将 ablated edges 置零，对大 circuit（100 edges）的破坏程度远大于\n      小 circuit（14 edges），因为更多路径被切断。这给了 CSS=1.0 (14 edges) 一个\n      不公平的优势——不是因为它的 edges 更好，而是因为 100-edge circuits 在 zero ablation\n      下 suffer disproportionately。Mean ablation 缓解了这个 bias（替换为 mean 而非 0），\n      导致大小 circuit 的 CPR 趋近。Resample ablation 进一步消除 out-of-distribution\n      artifacts。在 SVA 和 Arithmetic 上，即使在对 CSS 最有利的 zero ablation 下，\n      gradient methods 的高相关性也阻止了 CSS 产生优势。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: CSS advantage across ablation methods\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Task\", \"Zero Δ\", \"Mean Δ\", \"Resample Δ\"]\n          - [\"IOI\", \"+0.080\", \"+0.007\", \"+0.003\"]\n          - [\"SVA\", \"-0.020\", \"-0.070\", \"-0.070\"]\n          - [\"Arithmetic\", \"-0.053\", \"-0.066\", \"-0.070\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Grouped bar chart — CSS CPR advantage by ablation method × task，IOI 的 zero ablation 优势显眼但 mean/resample 下消失\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下此实验揭示 IOI positive result 的第二个 confound（除 ACDC isinf 外）：\n      zero ablation bias。这对 paper 是双刃剑——削弱了唯一的正面证据，\n      但为 analysis paper 提供了 \"evaluation method confounds in circuit faithfulness\"\n      的重要方法论贡献。建议在 paper 中诚实报告并讨论，这种 transparency 反而加分。\n\n  - name: \"CIRCUS as negative ablation\"\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      整理 D021 的 CIRCUS 三次失败结果，作为负面消融实验展示\n      structural consensus (CSS) vs faithfulness scoring (CIRCUS) 的区别。\n    expected_results:\n      circus_ioi_cpr: -0.108\n      circus_sva_cpr: -0.15\n      circus_arithmetic_cpr: -0.12\n      circus_failure_rate: \"3/3 tasks\"\n      css_vs_circus_framing: >\n        CIRCUS 在所有任务上 CPR 为负（比 random circuit 还差），\n        而 CSS 至少在 IOI 上为正。但 worst 档下 CSS 在 3/4 任务上也失败，\n        所以 CSS vs CIRCUS 的对比变成 \"both methods have severe limitations\"\n        而非 \"CSS > CIRCUS\"。\n    result_rationale: >\n      CIRCUS 使用 threshold diversity 在单一方法内部构建 consensus，\n      本质上是在同一 gradient landscape 上做不同切分——不提供新信息。\n      CSS 至少使用了不同方法，但当方法本身相关时也退化。\n      CIRCUS 的完全失败是可预期的：单方法 threshold sweep 生成的 \"diverse\" circuits\n      实际上是 nested sets（k=50 ⊂ k=100 ⊂ k=150），其交集就是最 conservative 的 cut，\n      这不是 consensus 而是 trivial intersection。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: CIRCUS vs CSS faithfulness comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Method\", \"IOI CPR\", \"SVA CPR\", \"Arith CPR\"]\n          - [\"CIRCUS\", \"-0.108\", \"-0.15\", \"-0.12\"]\n          - [\"CSS=1.0\", \"+0.109\", \"-0.05\", \"-0.184 (zero) / +0.919 (mean)\"]\n          - [\"Best single\", \"+0.029 (zero)\", \"+0.95 (mean)\", \"+0.985 (mean)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: CIRCUS vs CSS CPR across tasks — CIRCUS consistently negative, CSS mixed\"\n    analysis: >\n      CIRCUS 负面结果是 low-hanging fruit——容易写、审稿人会觉得有信息量。\n      在 analysis paper 中定位为 \"what definitely doesn't work\"，\n      与 CSS 的 \"works under specific conditions\" 形成对比。\n      0 GPU hours，纯分析工作，性价比最高的 planned 实验。\n\n  # === Jaccard Prediction ===\n  - name: \"Jaccard-CSS correlation analysis\"\n    plan_id: plan_013\n    description: >\n      跨所有 model×task 对，拟合 max pairwise Jaccard vs CSS faithfulness advantage 的关系。\n      Worst 档下数据点少且关系被 confound 驱动。\n    expected_results:\n      data_points:\n        - {task: \"IOI\", model: \"GPT-2\", max_jaccard: 0.31, css_advantage: 0.080, note: \"isinf ACDC, zero ablation\"}\n        - {task: \"Arithmetic\", model: \"GPT-2\", max_jaccard: 0.695, css_advantage: -0.066, note: \"mean ablation\"}\n        - {task: \"SVA\", model: \"GPT-2\", max_jaccard: 0.55, css_advantage: -0.070, note: \"mean ablation\"}\n        - {task: \"IOI\", model: \"Qwen-0.5B\", max_jaccard: 0.52, css_advantage: -0.020, note: \"with IFR\"}\n        - {task: \"Arithmetic\", model: \"Qwen-0.5B\", max_jaccard: 0.58, css_advantage: -0.070, note: \"with IFR\"}\n        - {task: \"IOI\", model: \"Gemma-2B\", max_jaccard: 0.48, css_advantage: -0.010, note: \"with IFR\"}\n      n_data_points: 6\n      spearman_rho: -0.54\n      spearman_p_value: 0.27\n      pearson_r: -0.61\n      pearson_p_value: 0.20\n      fitted_threshold: \"max_Jaccard < 0.35 for CSS to work\"\n      n_points_below_threshold: 1\n      n_points_above_threshold: 5\n      confound_analysis: >\n        去除 IOI GPT-2 (唯一用 ACDC isinf 且 zero ablation 的数据点) 后：\n        n=5, spearman_rho=-0.30, p=0.62。关系完全不显著。\n        IOI GPT-2 是 influential point (Cook's D > 1.0)，驱动了整个 correlation。\n    result_rationale: >\n      6 个数据点本身就 underpowered（Spearman 需 n≈10 才有检测 ρ=0.6 的 80% power）。\n      Worst 档下唯一的正面点 (IOI GPT-2) 同时有两个 confounds：\n      (1) ACDC isinf 压低了 max_Jaccard（top-k 归一化后 Jaccard 上升到 0.25→仍低，但方向变化）\n      (2) zero ablation 放大了 CSS 的 edge-efficiency 优势。\n      去除这个 influential point 后，剩余 5 个点都在 Jaccard 0.48-0.70 范围内，\n      CSS advantage 都在 [-0.07, -0.01] 范围内——flat line，no correlation。\n      Jaccard-utility 关系变成了 \"one-point story\"，统计上不可信。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Jaccard-CSS correlation data\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Task×Model\", \"Max Jaccard\", \"CSS Advantage\", \"Confounds\"]\n          - [\"IOI×GPT-2\", \"0.31\", \"+0.080\", \"ACDC isinf + zero ablation\"]\n          - [\"SVA×GPT-2\", \"0.55\", \"-0.070\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Arith×GPT-2\", \"0.695\", \"-0.066\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"IOI×Qwen\", \"0.52\", \"-0.020\", \"IFR may ≈ gradient\"]\n          - [\"Arith×Qwen\", \"0.58\", \"-0.070\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"IOI×Gemma\", \"0.48\", \"-0.010\", \"—\"]\n      - caption: \"Table: Correlation robustness\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Analysis\", \"ρ\", \"p-value\", \"n\"]\n          - [\"All points\", \"-0.54\", \"0.27\", \"6\"]\n          - [\"Remove IOI×GPT-2\", \"-0.30\", \"0.62\", \"5\"]\n          - [\"Remove ACDC tasks only\", \"-0.10\", \"0.87\", \"3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot — max Jaccard (x) vs CSS advantage (y)，IOI×GPT-2 是明显的 outlier，其余点 cluster 在右下区域\"\n      - \"Fig: Same scatter with IOI×GPT-2 标记为 hollow circle (confounded)，回归线变平\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档对 Claim 2 (CSS utility predicted by inter-method correlation) 的致命打击。\n      Correlation 在统计上不显著 (p=0.27)，且由单个 confounded data point 驱动。\n      Paper 不能声称 \"Jaccard predicts CSS utility\" 作为 empirical finding——\n      只能作为 \"motivated conjecture\" 或 \"necessary condition hypothesis\"。\n      Analysis paper 的重构方向：Jaccard 是 necessary condition check\n      （max_Jaccard > 0.5 → CSS almost certainly fails），\n      但不是 sufficient condition（max_Jaccard < 0.5 不保证 CSS works，\n      因为只有一个数据点且有 confounds）。\n      这限制了 contribution 的强度，但对 EMNLP Findings 或 workshop 仍可接受——\n      honest negative results 有其学术价值。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dc09ebfc-ff12-4d57-a5a3-2294962bcf00","total_cost_usd":0.5245420499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16597,"cache_read_input_tokens":54061,"output_tokens":13644,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16597,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":13310,"cache_read_input_tokens":21538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6900,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6900},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3820,"outputTokens":1430,"cacheReadInputTokens":63053,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28308,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0526603,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":13644,"cacheReadInputTokens":54061,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16597,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4718817499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7389b483-6b71-49fb-8688-bbb0ff20c49f"}
